<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Marketing Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Product marketing can become difficult when teams lack customer insight,
                    clear positioning, consistent messaging, or alignment between product and
                    commercial teams. Identifying these challenges early helps organizations
                    improve marketing effectiveness.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Unclear Product Positioning:</b> Define a focused value proposition that clearly communicates the product's unique benefits.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Weak Customer Understanding:</b> Use customer research, interviews, surveys, and feedback to improve marketing decisions.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Inconsistent Messaging:</b> Establish messaging guidelines so different teams communicate the same product value.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Low Campaign Performance:</b> Analyze customer engagement and continuously test messaging, content, and channels.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Poor Sales Alignment:</b> Provide sales teams with product information, competitive insights, presentations, and supporting materials.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Difficulty Measuring Impact:</b> Establish clear KPIs that connect marketing activity with product and business outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant challenge image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section>
